-- title:
--   Euler characteristic of the special fibre equals 1-g(X₁(Mp))
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M\ge 5$ a natural number with $p\nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$ and $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $L((q))$ obtained as the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $\mathbb{Q}$-rational $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$, and let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $A\subseteq L\subseteq K$. Let $j\in K$ be the element whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-function, and $j\neq0$. Let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $\Omega_0$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ which is an $A$-algebra with $\varpi\mapsto 0$. Finally let $\mathcal{W}$ consist of two affine open subsets $U_0,U_1$ of the base change $X\times_{\operatorname{Spec}A}\operatorname{Spec}\Omega_0$ of the two-chart integral model $X=\operatorname{TwoChartIntegralModel}$ of $K$ over $A$ with $j$, with $U_0\cup U_1$ the whole space and $U_0\cap U_1$ affine. Then, for the two-term Čech complex of the structure sheaf attached to this cover (sections over $U_0$ and $U_1$, differential the difference of restrictions to $U_0\cap U_1$, $H^0$ its kernel and $H^1$ the quotient of $\Gamma(U_0\cap U_1)$ by its image),
--   $$\dim_{\Omega_0}H^0-\dim_{\Omega_0}H^1 = 1-g,$$
--   where $g$ is [`AlgebraicCurve.genusFF`](def/AlgebraicCurve_Repartitions.html#L145) of the function field obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$, i.e. the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-dimension of the quotient of the repartitions by the sum of the repartitions of the zero divisor and the principal repartitions.
--
--   This is the arithmetic-genus computation for the geometric special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a discrete valuation ring above $p$ in $\mathbb{Z}[\zeta_p]$: the Čech Euler characteristic of the structure sheaf on the fibre is the same as on the generic fibre, namely $1-g(X_1(Mp))$. It feeds the subsequent analysis of the special fibre, being cited in the identification of non-regular points of the fibre and in the counting of points of the special fibre via the $j$-chart.
-- source:
